| GitHub Actions | ~48 min/day | 72% of 2,000/month |

## Content Pipeline (fetch_news.py)

```
Fetch (4 providers + 16 RSS) → Normalize → Deduplicate (3-layer) → Tag quality → Upload to Firebase
```

### Deduplication Layers
1. **Article ID hash** — SHA-256 of (normalized_title + normalized_source)
2. **URL dedup** — seen_urls set within RSS processing
3. **Cross-run cache** — `.article_cache.json` persisted via actions/cache

### Provider Tagging
Every article gets `_provider` key (`currentsapi` / `rss` / `newsdata` / `contextualweb` / `ai`).
Stripped before Firebase upload (explicit field mapping in `upload_articles`).

## Run Metrics (logs/run_metrics.csv)

Appended after every run. Columns:
`timestamp, tier, raw_total, within_run_dups, unique_this_run, cross_run_dups, fresh_unique, currentsapi, rss, newsdata, contextualweb, ai`

Committed and pushed by the workflow via `github-actions[bot]`.

